    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you mean about the adversity angle, but I'm still a bit worried. If we get too vague, they'll smell the spin. What if we were more direct? Could we actually say the project was a \"massive success that exceeded our baseline expectations\" or something similar? If we can convince them that the 5% was actually a huge win, it would secure that funding and save our mission. Is that too far, or is that the kind of language that makes the difference between getting the $5M or getting nothing?",
